{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathConstants","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathConstants","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.operationalEntropy_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.operationalEntropy_classical","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathConstants.lean#L166-L173","doc":"The operational entropy approaches 1 as q → 1.\nAt q = 1 exactly, η_q = (2·1 - 1) / 1^3 = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.speedOfLight_junk_at_classicality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.speedOfLight_junk_at_classicality","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathConstants.lean#L149-L164","doc":"**At classicality this declaration returns `0`, not a divergence.**\n\n`ArchimedeanSubstrateField` bounds `1 ≤ q`, so `q = 1` is permitted — it is the\nboundary of that bound, and the structure names it the classical limit. There the\ndenominator is `0` and Lean's `1/0 = 0`.\n\nStated as a theorem so the junk value is discoverable from the declaration itself\nrather than only from a reader's arithmetic, and so that `speedOfLight_positive`'s\n`q > 1` hypothesis reads as **load-bearing** rather than incidental: it is exactly\nthe hypothesis that excludes this point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.speedOfLight_positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.speedOfLight_positive","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathConstants.lean#L141-L147","doc":"The speed of light is positive when q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.gravitationalConstant_planck_units","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.gravitationalConstant_planck_units","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathConstants.lean#L131-L139","doc":"In Planck units, G_Planck = G(q) · (ℏ_q / c_q)^2 = 1 for all q > 1.\nThis expresses the fact that the gravitational constant, when measured\nin the natural units set by ℏ_q and c_q, is unity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.hausdorffDimension_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.hausdorffDimension_classical","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathConstants.lean#L88-L95","doc":"At classicality (q = 1), the Hausdorff dimension equals 1\n(the Julia set degenerates to the unit circle). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.gravitationalConstant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.gravitationalConstant","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathConstants.lean#L73-L84","doc":"**Gravitational constant** from jet tower entropy.\nG(q) = c_q^3 · ℏ_q / S_cell(q)\nwhere S_cell(q) = η_q · ℏ_q^2 / (1 - ℏ_q^2).\nLabel: def:gravitational-constant ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:gravitational-constant","label":"def:gravitational-constant","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/gravitational-constant.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.hausdorffDimension","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.hausdorffDimension","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathConstants.lean#L64-L69","doc":"**Hausdorff dimension** of the Julia set at substrate parameter q.\nd_H(q) = (2q - 1)^2 / q^3.\nLabel: rem:hausdorff-dimension-recurrence ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.operationalEntropy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.operationalEntropy","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathConstants.lean#L55-L60","doc":"**Operational entropy** at a point p ∈ M.\nη_q(p) = (2q(p) - 1) / q(p)^3.\nLabel: def:operational-entropy ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:operational-entropy","label":"def:operational-entropy","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/operational-entropy.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.speedOfLight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.speedOfLight","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathConstants.lean#L25-L51","doc":"**Speed of light** at a point p ∈ M.\nc_q(p) = 1 / (q(p) - 1).\nVanishes in the deep-quantum regime (q → ∞).\n\n**🛑 Carries content only for `q > 1`.** The docstring used to say this\n\"diverges at classicality (q → 1)\". As a statement about the mathematics that\nis right; as a statement about *this declaration* it is false, and in the\ndirection that matters. `ArchimedeanSubstrateField` requires `1 ≤ q`, so\n`q = 1` is not excluded — it is the **boundary** of the bound and the point\nthe structure's own docstring names \"the classical limit\". There\n`sp.field p - 1 = 0`, and Lean's `1/0 = 0`, so this returns **`0`**: the\nnumerically smallest possible value at exactly the point the prose says it\nblows up.\n\nRecorded as `speedOfLight_junk_at_classicality` below rather than left to a\nreader to discover. Every consumer in this file already hypothesises\n`q > 1`, so nothing downstream depends on the junk value.\n\nThe content-block sibling avoids this by construction: it takes the unit\n`d : kˣ` with `↑d = q − 1`, so at classicality the term cannot be formed at\nall. Reconciling the two is tracked separately; see\n`docs/audits/2026-09-05-the-archimedean-suffix-convention-is-the-wrong-instrument.md`.\n\nLabel: def:information-speed-of-light ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:information-speed-of-light","label":"def:information-speed-of-light","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/information-speed-of-light.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}